WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.049 --> 00:00:05.710
In 1997, former Saturday Night Live star Mike
Myers hit comedy gold with Austin Powers:

00:00:05.710 --> 00:00:10.710
International Man of Mystery, which was followed
by hit sequels in 1999 and 2002.

00:00:10.710 --> 00:00:14.920
But despite the massive popularity and box
office success of the franchise, and the fact

00:00:14.920 --> 00:00:19.759
that everyone involved wants to make another
movie, we're still waiting for the next installment…

00:00:19.759 --> 00:00:21.160
and we may have to keep waiting.

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:25.590
Here's a look at why we never got to see Austin
Powers 4.

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:26.689
Development hell

00:00:26.689 --> 00:00:31.179
The Austin Powers franchise generated a ton
of revenue for New Line Cinema, money which

00:00:31.179 --> 00:00:34.399
the studio invested in films like the Lord
of the Rings trilogy.

00:00:34.399 --> 00:00:39.079
But while that should have ensured them footing
for Austin Powers 4, New Line Cinema got themselves

00:00:39.079 --> 00:00:43.489
in a world of financial trouble with expensive
flops like The Golden Compass and through

00:00:43.489 --> 00:00:47.210
public accounting disputes with Lord of the
Rings mastermind Peter Jackson.

00:00:47.210 --> 00:00:51.390
All of which led to New Line Cinema pushing
hard for Austin Powers 4 in order to shore

00:00:51.390 --> 00:00:52.579
up their sinking ship.

00:00:52.579 --> 00:00:56.879
But before it could get made, the studio went
under and was bought out by Warner Bros.

00:00:56.879 --> 00:01:00.699
No wonder development on Austin Powers 4 has
stalled indefinitely.

00:01:00.699 --> 00:01:03.390
Austin Powers 3 wasn't...good

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.420
The first two Austin Powers movies saw the
character move from cult phenom to blockbuster

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:13.630
franchise star, spoofing James Bond while
adding a slew of new catchphrases to our vocabulary.

00:01:15.060 --> 00:01:18.280
"One MILLION dollars!"

00:01:18.280 --> 00:01:23.280
But despite being a financial success, the
third film, Austin Powers in Goldmember, didn't

00:01:23.280 --> 00:01:25.420
quite live up to the reputation of its predecessors.

00:01:25.420 --> 00:01:30.350
It opened to middling reviews, thanks in part
to an overreliance on pop culture jokes of

00:01:30.350 --> 00:01:32.780
the era, which have not aged well at all.

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:34.310
A Britney Spears cameo?

00:01:34.310 --> 00:01:36.720
A Silence of the Lambs parody?

00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:38.470
A scene with the Osbournes?

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:43.590
With Goldmember, Austin Powers lost some of
his mojo, meaning fans haven't exactly been

00:01:43.590 --> 00:01:45.590
demanding a fourth film.

00:01:45.590 --> 00:01:47.320
Career downturn

00:01:47.320 --> 00:01:51.380
Between Austin Powers and Shrek, there was
a time when Mike Myers couldn't do anything

00:01:51.380 --> 00:01:52.380
wrong.

00:01:52.380 --> 00:01:55.980
Unfortunately for him and his fans, that time
was more than a decade ago.

00:01:55.980 --> 00:02:00.140
Since then, it's been a rocky road for Myers,
both professionally and personally.

00:02:00.140 --> 00:02:05.070
In 2005, Myers and his wife Robin, who he
had described as his "muse" and who urged

00:02:05.070 --> 00:02:08.890
him to write the first Austin Powers film
to begin with, divorced.

00:02:08.890 --> 00:02:14.270
And the one-time star suffered a string of
box office and critical bombs, including 2008's

00:02:14.270 --> 00:02:19.030
The Love Guru — which as of the time of
this video, is still the last major film role

00:02:19.030 --> 00:02:20.690
Myers has taken on.

00:02:20.690 --> 00:02:25.200
Considering it's been nearly a decade since
Myers has made any movie, the chances of Austin

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:28.260
Powers 4 happening at this point seem very
remote indeed.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:29.260
"Right.

00:02:29.260 --> 00:02:31.120
Okay, people, you have to tell me these things,
alright?

00:02:31.120 --> 00:02:34.550
I've been frozen for thirty years, okay?!

00:02:34.550 --> 00:02:37.870
Throw me a frickin' bone here!"

00:02:39.410 --> 00:02:41.069
The Animated Hold Up

00:02:41.069 --> 00:02:45.420
So how cool would it be to see a TV series
that mixed the best parts of both Shrek and

00:02:45.420 --> 00:02:46.440
Austin Powers?

00:02:46.440 --> 00:02:50.330
That might sound like a pipe dream, but it
came very close to happening after Myers cut

00:02:50.330 --> 00:02:55.281
a deal with HBO for an animated Austin Powers
series featuring Myers as the voice of both

00:02:55.281 --> 00:02:57.230
Austin Powers and Dr. Evil.

00:02:57.230 --> 00:03:01.980
HBO commissioned a 13-episode season, which
was going to feature the kind of adult-themed

00:03:01.980 --> 00:03:04.850
content you would expect to see on an HBO
cartoon.

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:09.480
Myers even hinted at the possibility of an
animated prequel origin film for Austin Powers

00:03:09.480 --> 00:03:10.480
as well.

00:03:10.480 --> 00:03:12.610
And then, well, nothing happened.

00:03:12.610 --> 00:03:17.570
HBO quietly cancelled the series, and though
neither the network nor Myers has ever confirmed

00:03:17.570 --> 00:03:21.550
why, writer Eric Goldman has hinted that Myers
backed out of the project.

00:03:21.550 --> 00:03:24.640
Well, we thought that was a good idea, even
if Myers didn't.

00:03:24.640 --> 00:03:26.900
"Dr. Evil, I love your plan."

00:03:26.900 --> 00:03:28.020
"Ja, eh?"

00:03:28.020 --> 00:03:29.720
"Ja, Herr Doktor.

00:03:29.720 --> 00:03:31.870
It's a REALLY good plan."

00:03:31.870 --> 00:03:34.459
It still could happen...

00:03:34.459 --> 00:03:38.440
Despite all the hold-ups and dead ends the
franchise has suffered so far, it's possible

00:03:38.440 --> 00:03:43.170
that there will eventually be an Austin Powers
4 for one simple reason: Myers says he still

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:44.290
wants to make it.

00:03:44.290 --> 00:03:48.460
In fact, he's been pretty consistent on this
point, telling the press in 2007, 2010, and

00:03:48.460 --> 00:03:53.180
2016 that he was still working on the film.

00:03:53.180 --> 00:03:57.910
Exactly what Austin Powers 4 will look like
when it finally arrives is unknown, though

00:03:57.910 --> 00:04:01.880
at one point, Myers said the next film will
focus on Dr. Evil's relationship with his

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.050
son, Scott Evil.

00:04:03.050 --> 00:04:07.040
"Well, don't look at me like I'm frickin'
Frankenstein, give your father a hug."

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.880
And director Jay Roach, who helmed the first
three films, has said he also wants to be

00:04:10.880 --> 00:04:14.040
involved, which would make it a true Austin
Powers reunion.

00:04:14.040 --> 00:04:19.629
"You know, Mike gave me the break of a lifetime
in letting me direct Austin 1.

00:04:19.629 --> 00:04:21.459
So I'm always good to go…"

00:04:21.459 --> 00:04:24.479
"You have any ideas about what 4 would be
like?"

00:04:24.479 --> 00:04:28.169
Well, Larry, probably something a lot like...this:

00:04:28.169 --> 00:04:30.759
"Oh, behave.

00:04:30.759 --> 00:04:32.059
Yeah.

00:04:32.059 --> 00:04:33.699
Yeah, baby!

00:04:33.720 --> 00:04:35.019
Yeah!"

00:04:35.949 --> 00:04:36.949
And also this:

00:04:36.949 --> 00:04:38.569
"Get in my belly!"

00:04:38.569 --> 00:04:41.550
And of course, lots and lots of this:

00:04:41.550 --> 00:04:45.960
"Welcome to my new submarine lair.

00:04:45.960 --> 00:04:49.000
It's long and hard and full of seamen!"

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:55.020
"Nothing?

00:04:55.180 --> 00:04:55.680
No?

00:04:55.840 --> 00:04:57.660
Not even a titter?

00:04:57.669 --> 00:04:58.669
Tough sub."

00:04:58.669 --> 00:04:59.669
Thanks for watching!

